[4] Readout
  HYP-2975 is not a standalone proof.  It contributes a local boundary
  curvature audit inside HYP-2970's endpoint-credit graph.
  Positive safe intervals are visible as bridges; AP/GW are zero-open but
  leave isolated taut vertices with mod-14 zero-sum endpoint transfers.
  The falsifier to search for is a primitive qdiv>=14 row with no positive
  bridge, no AP/GW taut current, and no K33/state-lift or Toeplitz-negative
  exit.  The bounded bank scanned here found none.
